  "prompt": "Load the Chicago ZIP boundary polygons from the Data Catalog, keep the downtown ZIPs (the Loop and its neighbours), and add each ZIP's area in square kilometres, measured in a projected coordinate system. Draw the frame as an Autark map coloured by area, and next to it the same map in Vega-Lite. Then show the same pair of maps three more times: once from a plain DataFrame that still holds the geometry column, once from a DataFrame with the geometry dropped (both views should say there is nothing to draw), and once from the frame reprojected to Illinois East. Also make a second layer with a point at the centre of each ZIP and draw the polygons and the points together on one Autark map. Finally add a bar chart of area by ZIP, linked to the first Autark map so that hovering a bar highlights its ZIP.",
